{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And YHWH appeared to Abram.</b> The reason YHWH did not appear to him immediately when He said to him 'Go forth from your land' is that at that time he was still outside the Land, according to the opinion of the Ibn Ezra, and outside the Land His Shekhinah, may He be blessed, does not reveal itself — and a proof is from Yonah (Mekhilta Bo 12d). If so, YHWH did not appear to him there in a vision, but only a voice of words did he hear alone; therefore he did not build an altar there, but only 'to YHWH who appeared to him' (Genesis 12:7). But as long as He had not appeared to him, he did not wish to build an altar in a place where the Shekhinah does not dwell. And this is what is said of Moses: 'For they will say, YHWH has not appeared to you' (Exodus 4:1) — for it is not His way to appear outside the Land; and on this basis they would also deny him, saying that not even a voice did you hear."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:28:03.839091314Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}